---
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import RelatedTools from '../components/RelatedTools.astro';
import { toolBySlug } from '../data/tools';

const tool = toolBySlug['startup-valuation-calculator'];
const breadcrumbItems = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: tool.title }];
const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Startup Valuation: Methods, Multiples & Free Calculator",
    "description": "Learn the Berkus, Scorecard, and VC methods for valuing startups. Understand pre-money vs post-money valuation and use our free calculator to estimate your startup's worth.",
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "FreeOnlineToolkit" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "FreeOnlineToolkit" },
    "datePublished": "2025-01-01",
    "dateModified": "2025-01-01",
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    "name": "How to Estimate Your Startup Valuation",
    "description": "Calculate your startup's pre-money and post-money valuation using Berkus, Scorecard, and VC methods.",
    "step": [
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "text": "Select a valuation method (Berkus, Scorecard, or VC Method)" },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "text": "Enter your annual revenue and revenue growth rate" },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "text": "Rate your team quality, product stage, market size, and competitive position" },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "text": "Enter the investment amount you are seeking" },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "text": "Review your pre-money and post-money valuation estimates" },
    ],
  },
];
---

<ToolLayout title="Startup Valuation: Methods, Multiples & Free Calculator — FreeOnlineToolkit" description="Learn the Berkus, Scorecard, and VC methods for valuing startups. Use our free calculator to estimate your startup's worth." breadcrumbItems={breadcrumbItems} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <fragment slot="heading"><h1>Startup Valuation: Methods, Multiples & Free Calculator</h1></fragment>
  <fragment slot="intro">
    <div class="key-takeaways">
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Startup valuation is more <strong>art than science</strong> at early stages — use multiple methods to get a valuation range, not a single number</li>
        <li>The <strong>Berkus method</strong> works best for pre-revenue startups, assigning up to $500K per category (idea, prototype, team, relationships, sales)</li>
        <li>The <strong>Scorecard method</strong> compares your startup to regional averages, weighting team (30%) and product (25%) most heavily</li>
        <li>The <strong>VC method</strong> projects revenue 5 years out, applies industry multiples (SaaS 5×, Fintech 4×), and discounts at a 10× target return</li>
        <li>Seed-stage pre-money valuations typically range from <strong>$2M to $10M</strong> depending on traction, team, and market size</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p>One of the most challenging questions a startup founder faces is: "What is my company worth?" Unlike public companies with transparent market prices, startup valuation is inherently uncertain. There are no earnings reports, no trading history, and often no revenue to anchor the analysis. Yet valuation matters enormously — it determines how much equity you give up when raising capital, sets expectations for future rounds, and influences how investors perceive your business. Understanding valuation methods gives founders a critical advantage in fundraising negotiations.</p>

    <p>Startup valuation depends heavily on the stage of the company. <strong>Pre-revenue startups</strong> (those that have not yet generated sales) are valued based on qualitative factors: the strength of the founding team, the size of the addressable market, the quality of the product or prototype, and the competitive landscape. <strong>Revenue-generating startups</strong> can be valued using financial metrics like revenue multiples, which compare your annual revenue to what similar companies have been valued at. The higher your growth rate, the higher the multiple investors will apply.</p>

    <p>The three most widely used early-stage valuation methods each take a different approach. The <strong>Berkus method</strong>, developed by angel investor Dave Berkus, assigns dollar values to five risk categories for pre-revenue companies. The <strong>Scorecard method</strong> (Bill Payne method) starts with a regional baseline valuation and adjusts based on how your startup compares to average companies across weighted factors. The <strong>VC method</strong> works backward from a projected exit value, applying a target return multiple to determine what the company is worth today. Using all three methods gives you a realistic range to present to investors.</p>

    <p>A critical distinction in fundraising is between <strong>pre-money</strong> and <strong>post-money</strong> valuation. Pre-money is what your company is worth before the investment. Post-money is pre-money plus the investment amount. If your pre-money valuation is $4M and you raise $1M, your post-money is $5M and the investor gets 20% ownership ($1M ÷ $5M). This math is fundamental to understanding dilution and negotiating fair terms.</p>
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="calculator">
    <div class="calc-card">
      <h2>Valuation Estimator</h2>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="valuationMethod">Method</label>
        <select id="valuationMethod" onchange="switchValuationMethod()">
          <option value="berkus">Berkus Method</option>
          <option value="scorecard" selected>Scorecard Method</option>
          <option value="vc">VC Method</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="form-row">
        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="annualRevenue">Annual Revenue ($)</label>
          <div class="input-wrap">
            <span class="prefix">$</span>
            <input type="number" id="annualRevenue" class="prefixed" value="500000" min="0" step="10000">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
          <label for="revenueGrowth">Revenue Growth Rate (%)</label>
          <input type="number" id="revenueGrowth" value="50" min="0" step="5">
          <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-top:3px;display:block;">Year over year %</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="industrySelect">Industry</label>
        <select id="industrySelect">
          <option value="saas">SaaS</option>
          <option value="fintech">Fintech</option>
          <option value="healthtech">HealthTech</option>
          <option value="ecommerce">E-commerce</option>
          <option value="other">Other</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div id="scorecardFields">
        <div class="form-row">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="teamQuality">Team Quality (1-5)</label>
            <input type="number" id="teamQuality" value="3" min="1" max="5" step="1">
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="productStage">Product Stage (1-5)</label>
            <input type="number" id="productStage" value="3" min="1" max="5" step="1">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="form-row">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="marketSize">Market Size (1-5)</label>
            <input type="number" id="marketSize" value="3" min="1" max="5" step="1">
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="competitivePos">Competitive Position (1-5)</label>
            <input type="number" id="competitivePos" value="3" min="1" max="5" step="1">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group" id="investmentField" style="display:none;">
        <label for="investmentAmount">Investment Amount Sought ($)</label>
        <div class="input-wrap">
          <span class="prefix">$</span>
          <input type="number" id="investmentAmount" class="prefixed" value="500000" min="0" step="50000">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="btn-group">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" id="calcBtn" data-i18n="common.calculate">Calculate</button>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="resetBtn" data-i18n="common.reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="result-box" id="valuationResult">
        <div class="val-panel" id="berkusPanel">
          <div class="result-value" id="berkusTotal">$0</div>
          <div class="result-label">Pre-Money Valuation (Berkus Method)</div>
          <div class="result-details">
            <div><span class="label">Sound Idea</span><span class="value" id="berkusIdea">$0</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Quality Prototype</span><span class="value" id="berkusPrototype">$0</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Quality Team</span><span class="value" id="berkusTeam">$0</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Strategic Relationships</span><span class="value" id="berkusStrategic">$0</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Product Rollout / Sales</span><span class="value" id="berkusSales">$0</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="val-panel" id="scorecardPanel">
          <div class="result-value" id="scorecardValue">$0</div>
          <div class="result-label">Pre-Money Valuation (Scorecard Method)</div>
          <div class="result-details">
            <div><span class="label">Relative Comparison</span><span class="value" id="scorecardComparison">0.0 out of 5</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="rate-breakdown" style="margin-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:10px;">Factor Scores</h3>
            <div class="factor-bar"><span class="f-label">Team (30%)</span><span class="f-score" id="scFactorTeam">0.0</span></div>
            <div class="factor-bar"><span class="f-label">Product (25%)</span><span class="f-score" id="scFactorProduct">0.0</span></div>
            <div class="factor-bar"><span class="f-label">Market (10%)</span><span class="f-score" id="scFactorMarket">0.0</span></div>
            <div class="factor-bar"><span class="f-label">Competitive (15%)</span><span class="f-score" id="scFactorCompetitive">0.0</span></div>
            <div class="factor-bar"><span class="f-label">Other (20%)</span><span class="f-score" id="scFactorOther">0.0</span></div>
            <div class="factor-bar" style="border-bottom:none;font-weight:600;"><span class="f-label">Weighted Average</span><span class="f-score" id="scWeightedAvg" style="color:var(--color-primary-dark);">0.0</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="val-panel" id="vcPanel">
          <div class="result-value" id="vcPreMoney">$0</div>
          <div class="result-label">Pre-Money Valuation (VC Method)</div>
          <div class="result-details">
            <div><span class="label">Terminal Value (Year 5)</span><span class="value" id="vcTerminalValue">$0</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Target Return</span><span class="value" id="vcTargetReturn">10x</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Post-Money Valuation</span><span class="value" id="vcPostMoney">$0</span></div>
            <div><span class="label">Investment Amount</span><span class="value" id="vcInvestment">$0</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="content">
    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>What This Calculator Shows</h2>
      <p>This calculator estimates your startup's pre-money valuation using three industry-standard methods. The <strong>Berkus method</strong> shows a breakdown across five value categories. The <strong>Scorecard method</strong> shows your weighted comparison to regional averages. The <strong>VC method</strong> projects your terminal value, post-money valuation, and implied pre-money based on a 10× target return. Use all three to triangulate a realistic valuation range for investor conversations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>How to Use</h2>
      <p>Select a valuation method and enter your startup's key metrics. Each method uses different inputs:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Berkus Method</strong> &mdash; best for pre-revenue startups. Assigns up to $500K to each of five value categories (sound idea, prototype, team, strategic relationships, sales). Total capped at $2.5M.</li>
        <li><strong>Scorecard Method</strong> &mdash; compares your startup to average companies in your region. Uses weighted factors: team (30%), product (25%), market (10%), competitive position (15%), and other (20%). Based on a $2M baseline.</li>
        <li><strong>VC Method</strong> &mdash; calculates valuation by projecting revenue 5 years out, applying an industry multiple, and discounting back at a 10x target return.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Enter your annual revenue, growth rate, and industry for all methods. The extra fields adapt based on your selected method. Use all three to get a valuation range rather than a single number.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Valuation Methods Explained</h2>
      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:12px 0 6px;">Berkus Method</h3>
      <p>Developed by angel investor Dave Berkus for pre-revenue startups. Assigns up to $500K to each of five risk categories, with a maximum of $2.5M. The actual amount per category depends on how strongly your startup scores in each area.</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:12px 0 6px;">Scorecard Method</h3>
      <p>Also called the Bill Payne method. Starts with the average pre-money valuation for seed-stage startups in your region ($2M baseline), then adjusts it based on how your startup compares to the average across five weighted factors.</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:12px 0 6px;">VC Method</h3>
      <p>Projects your startup's revenue 5 years into the future using your growth rate, applies an industry-specific revenue multiple to calculate terminal value, then discounts back using a 10x target return. Industry multiples: SaaS 5.0x, Fintech 4.0x, HealthTech 3.0x, E-commerce 2.0x, Other 3.0x.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Next Steps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Run all three methods</strong> and present a valuation range (e.g., "$3M - $5M based on Berkus, Scorecard, and VC methods") to investors</li>
        <li><strong>Gather comparable data</strong> — research recent seed or Series A valuations in your industry and region to benchmark your estimates</li>
        <li><strong>Focus on the team score</strong> — investors weight the founding team more heavily than any other factor at early stages</li>
        <li><strong>Prepare your pitch</strong> with a clear narrative around your market size, traction, and competitive moat to justify your target valuation</li>
        <li><strong>Be flexible</strong> — valuation is negotiated, not calculated. Use these numbers as a starting point, not a demand</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <FAQ items={[
      { question: "What is the difference between pre-money and post-money valuation?", answer: "Pre-money valuation is the value of your startup before receiving new investment. Post-money valuation is pre-money plus the investment amount. For example, if your pre-money valuation is $4M and you raise $1M, your post-money valuation is $5M. The investor gets 20% ownership ($1M / $5M)." },
      { question: "Which valuation method is most accurate for early-stage startups?", answer: "No single method is perfectly accurate for early-stage startups. The Berkus method works well for pre-revenue startups with significant risk. The Scorecard method is best when you have some traction and comparable companies. The VC method is most useful when you have revenue data and a clear exit strategy. Use all three to get a valuation range." },
      { question: "How does industry affect startup valuation?", answer: "Industry affects valuation through comparable company multiples and market size. SaaS companies typically command higher multiples (5x revenue) due to recurring revenue and scalability. Fintech averages 4x, HealthTech 3x, and E-commerce 2x. Larger addressable markets also support higher valuations." },
      { question: "What is a reasonable pre-money valuation for a seed-stage startup?", answer: "Seed-stage pre-money valuations typically range from $2M to $10M depending on team quality, traction, market size, and investor demand. The average seed round in the US is around $6-8M pre-money as of 2025. Pre-revenue startups tend to fall in the $2-5M range, while those with revenue may reach $5-10M+." },
    ]} />
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="sidebar">
    <RelatedTools currentSlug="startup-valuation-calculator" category="business-finance" />
  </fragment>
</ToolLayout>

<script>
import { getNum, formatCurrency, showResult, hideResult } from '../utils/calculator-utils';

function switchValuationMethod() {
  const method = (document.getElementById('valuationMethod') as HTMLSelectElement).value;
  const fields = document.getElementById('scorecardFields')!;
  const invField = document.getElementById('investmentField')!;

  fields.style.display = (method === 'scorecard' || method === 'berkus') ? 'block' : 'none';
  invField.style.display = (method === 'vc') ? 'block' : 'none';

  if (document.getElementById('valuationResult')!.classList.contains('visible')) {
    calcValuation();
  }
}

function calcValuation() {
  const method = (document.getElementById('valuationMethod') as HTMLSelectElement).value;
  let revenue = getNum('annualRevenue');
  let growth = getNum('revenueGrowth');
  const industry = (document.getElementById('industrySelect') as HTMLSelectElement).value;

  if (!revenue || revenue < 0) { revenue = 0; (document.getElementById('annualRevenue') as HTMLInputElement).value = '0'; }
  if (!growth || growth < 0) { growth = 0; (document.getElementById('revenueGrowth') as HTMLInputElement).value = '0'; }

  document.getElementById('berkusPanel')!.classList.remove('visible');
  document.getElementById('scorecardPanel')!.classList.remove('visible');
  document.getElementById('vcPanel')!.classList.remove('visible');

  if (method === 'berkus') {
    calcBerkus();
  } else if (method === 'scorecard') {
    calcScorecard();
  } else if (method === 'vc') {
    calcVCMethod(revenue, growth, industry);
  }

  showResult('valuationResult');
}

function calcBerkus() {
  let teamScore = getNum('teamQuality');
  let productScore = getNum('productStage');
  let marketScore = getNum('marketSize');
  let compScore = getNum('competitivePos');

  if (!teamScore || teamScore < 1) { teamScore = 3; (document.getElementById('teamQuality') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }
  if (!productScore || productScore < 1) { productScore = 3; (document.getElementById('productStage') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }
  if (!marketScore || marketScore < 1) { marketScore = 3; (document.getElementById('marketSize') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }
  if (!compScore || compScore < 1) { compScore = 3; (document.getElementById('competitivePos') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }

  const maxPerCategory = 500000;
  const ideaVal = maxPerCategory;
  const prototypeVal = (productScore / 5) * maxPerCategory;
  const teamVal = (teamScore / 5) * maxPerCategory;
  const strategicVal = (marketScore / 5) * maxPerCategory;
  const salesVal = (compScore / 5) * maxPerCategory;
  const total = ideaVal + prototypeVal + teamVal + strategicVal + salesVal;

  document.getElementById('berkusIdea')!.textContent = formatCurrency(ideaVal);
  document.getElementById('berkusPrototype')!.textContent = formatCurrency(prototypeVal);
  document.getElementById('berkusTeam')!.textContent = formatCurrency(teamVal);
  document.getElementById('berkusStrategic')!.textContent = formatCurrency(strategicVal);
  document.getElementById('berkusSales')!.textContent = formatCurrency(salesVal);
  document.getElementById('berkusTotal')!.textContent = formatCurrency(total);
  document.getElementById('berkusPanel')!.classList.add('visible');
}

function calcScorecard() {
  let teamScore = getNum('teamQuality');
  let productScore = getNum('productStage');
  let marketScore = getNum('marketSize');
  let compScore = getNum('competitivePos');

  if (!teamScore || teamScore < 1) { teamScore = 3; (document.getElementById('teamQuality') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }
  if (!productScore || productScore < 1) { productScore = 3; (document.getElementById('productStage') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }
  if (!marketScore || marketScore < 1) { marketScore = 3; (document.getElementById('marketSize') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }
  if (!compScore || compScore < 1) { compScore = 3; (document.getElementById('competitivePos') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3'; }

  const teamFactor = teamScore / 5;
  const productFactor = productScore / 5;
  const marketFactor = marketScore / 5;
  const compFactor = compScore / 5;
  const otherFactor = 0.5;

  const weightedAvg = (teamFactor * 0.30) + (productFactor * 0.25) + (marketFactor * 0.10) + (compFactor * 0.15) + (otherFactor * 0.20);
  const baseline = 2000000;
  const preMoney = baseline * weightedAvg;
  const overallScore = weightedAvg * 5;

  document.getElementById('scFactorTeam')!.textContent = teamFactor.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById('scFactorProduct')!.textContent = productFactor.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById('scFactorMarket')!.textContent = marketFactor.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById('scFactorCompetitive')!.textContent = compFactor.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById('scFactorOther')!.textContent = otherFactor.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById('scWeightedAvg')!.textContent = weightedAvg.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById('scorecardComparison')!.textContent = overallScore.toFixed(1) + ' out of 5';
  document.getElementById('scorecardValue')!.textContent = formatCurrency(preMoney);
  document.getElementById('scorecardPanel')!.classList.add('visible');
}

function calcVCMethod(revenue: number, growth: number, industry: string) {
  let investment = getNum('investmentAmount');
  if (!investment || investment < 0) { investment = 0; (document.getElementById('investmentAmount') as HTMLInputElement).value = '0'; }

  const multiples: Record<string, number> = { saas: 5, fintech: 4, healthtech: 3, ecommerce: 2, other: 3 };
  const multiple = multiples[industry] || 3;
  const growthDecimal = growth / 100;
  const projectedRevenue = revenue * Math.pow(1 + growthDecimal, 5);
  const terminalValue = projectedRevenue * multiple;
  const targetReturn = 10;
  const postMoney = terminalValue / targetReturn;
  const preMoney = Math.max(0, postMoney - investment);

  document.getElementById('vcTerminalValue')!.textContent = formatCurrency(terminalValue);
  document.getElementById('vcTargetReturn')!.textContent = targetReturn + 'x';
  document.getElementById('vcPostMoney')!.textContent = formatCurrency(postMoney);
  document.getElementById('vcInvestment')!.textContent = formatCurrency(investment);
  document.getElementById('vcPreMoney')!.textContent = formatCurrency(preMoney);
  document.getElementById('vcPanel')!.classList.add('visible');
}

function resetValuation() {
  (document.getElementById('valuationMethod') as HTMLSelectElement).value = 'scorecard';
  (document.getElementById('annualRevenue') as HTMLInputElement).value = '500000';
  (document.getElementById('revenueGrowth') as HTMLInputElement).value = '50';
  (document.getElementById('industrySelect') as HTMLSelectElement).value = 'saas';
  (document.getElementById('teamQuality') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3';
  (document.getElementById('productStage') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3';
  (document.getElementById('marketSize') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3';
  (document.getElementById('competitivePos') as HTMLInputElement).value = '3';
  (document.getElementById('investmentAmount') as HTMLInputElement).value = '500000';
  document.getElementById('scorecardFields')!.style.display = 'block';
  document.getElementById('investmentField')!.style.display = 'none';
  document.getElementById('berkusPanel')!.classList.remove('visible');
  document.getElementById('scorecardPanel')!.classList.remove('visible');
  document.getElementById('vcPanel')!.classList.remove('visible');
  hideResult('valuationResult');
}

document.getElementById('calcBtn')!.addEventListener('click', calcValuation);
document.getElementById('resetBtn')!.addEventListener('click', resetValuation);
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
  switchValuationMethod();
  calcValuation();
});
</script>

<style>
.val-panel { display: none; }
.val-panel.visible { display: block; }
.factor-bar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 6px 0;
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
}
.factor-bar:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.factor-bar .f-label { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
.factor-bar .f-score { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-primary); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
</style>
